{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.mkForallFVarsS\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkForallFVarsS</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">xs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/SymM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM\">SymM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Similar to `mkForallFVars`, but uses the more efficient `abstractFVars` and `abstractFVarsPrefix`,\nand makes the same assumption made by these functions.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.mkForallFVarsS","kind":"def","line":126,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.mkForallFVarsS","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.lean#L126-L136"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.mkLambdaFVarsS\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkLambdaFVarsS</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">xs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/SymM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM\">SymM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Similar to `mkLambdaFVars`, but uses the more efficient `abstractFVars` and `abstractFVarsPrefix`,\nand makes the same assumption made by these functions.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.mkLambdaFVarsS","kind":"def","line":114,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.mkLambdaFVarsS","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.lean#L114-L124"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVars\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">abstractFVars</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">xs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/SymM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM\">SymM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Abstracts free variables `xs` in expression `e`, converting them to de Bruijn indices.\n\nIt is an abbreviation for `abstractFVarsRange e 0 xs`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVars","kind":"def","line":106,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVars","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.lean#L106-L112"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVarsPrefix\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">abstractFVarsPrefix</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">xs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/SymM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM\">SymM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Abstracts free variables `xs[0...n)` in expression `e`, converting them to de Bruijn indices:\n`xs[n-1]` becomes `#0`, ..., `xs[0]` becomes `#(n-1)`. This is the `Sym` counterpart of\n`Expr.abstractRange`, and it is the operation needed for the type of the binder `xs[n]` when\nrebuilding a telescope.\n\nMakes the same assumptions as `abstractFVarsRange`; the minimal variable must be `xs[0]`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVarsPrefix","kind":"def","line":80,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVarsPrefix","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.lean#L80-L104"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVarsRange\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">abstractFVarsRange</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">start</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">xs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/SymM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM\">SymM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Abstracts free variables `xs[start...*]` in expression `e`, converting them to de Bruijn indices.\n\nAssumptions:\n- The local context of the metavariables occurring in `e` do not include the free variables being\n  abstracted. This invariant holds when abstracting over binders during pattern matching/unification:\n  metavariables in the pattern were created before entering the binder, so their contexts exclude\n  the bound variable's corresponding fvar.\n\n- If `xs[start...*]` is not empty, then the minimal variable is `xs[start]`.\n\n- Subterms whose `maxFVar` is below `minFVarId` are skipped entirely. This function does not assume\nthe `maxFVar` cache contains information for every subterm in `e`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVarsRange","kind":"def","line":50,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.abstractFVarsRange","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/AbstractS.lean#L50-L78"}}],"imports":["Init.Omega","Lean.Meta.Sym.ReplaceS","Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.AbstractS"}